+\paragraph{Re-evaluation evidence.} Checks cover a PPO baseline, a PPO hover-bonus policy and a DQN baseline.
+Windows CI and recording-machine evaluations match all 300 episodes on five summary fields: length,
+original/training return, environment outcome and strict landing. On Linux, summaries differ; mean-return
+differences are at most 1.52, with strict landing rates unchanged at 96\%, 0\% and 29\%. Individual
+original-return differences reach 0.28, 11.9 and 192. Holm-corrected paired tests detect no aggregate
+difference; this screen does not establish equivalence. Nine open-loop traces show early simulator-state
+differences without greedy-action changes on recorded observations, supporting a simulator-numerics
+explanation. These checks concern three policies and selected traces; they do not identify a unique compiler cause.
 
